21. NON-NEGOTIABLE ACTIVE RULES

HOMIO must look like a major global real-estate platform, not a single-broker website.

The single-broker operating model remains internal, not the public identity.

Basic builder/project listing can be free.

HOMIO-originated transactions must have clear pre-agreed commercial terms.

Premium visibility remains monetizable even when basic listing is free.

Raw lead resale must not be the core value proposition.

Qualified and attributable demand is more valuable than raw lead count.

Lead ownership and attribution must be traceable in REOS.

Lead qualification, matching and repetitive follow-up should become progressively autonomous.

Human intervention should focus on high-value opportunities and exceptions.

Advertising must complement, not damage, the user experience.

Services and partner revenue can create additional monetization layers.

SaaS/enterprise should create recurring revenue independent of individual transactions.

Frontend remains consumer-first and marketplace-like.

REOS remains the operating system and authority layer.

Do not create duplicate lead, transaction, commission or governance engines.

Global brokerage execution must remain legally adaptable by jurisdiction.

The platform must scale beyond the manual capacity of one broker through automation.

Public messaging must sell the platform and user value, not the personal identity of the broker.

The system must optimize for qualified revenue opportunities, not vanity lead volume.

22. FINAL NORTH-STAR STATEMENT

HOMIO acquires global real-estate demand through a marketplace experience, converts that demand into qualified and attributable opportunities through autonomous technology, operates a controlled brokerage workflow, monetizes successful transactions, and adds recurring revenue through builders, advertising, services and SaaS — while presenting publicly as a global real-estate technology platform rather than a single-broker website.

